he was one of the greatest aviators of  his generation  u.s pilot chuck yeager started off as an  aircraft mechanic before becoming a  world war  ii fighter ace and the first person to  break the sound barrier  charles yeager climbs down into the  cockpit of the rocket craft  it was on october 1947 and at the age of  24 that he flew an airplane through the  sound barrier at a speed of more than a  thousand kilometers an hour  such attempts had killed other pilots  before  he would later say he could have gone  even faster had the plane carried more  fuel  but he did continue to fly faster on  other dangerous missions  his tests were used by the u.s air force  and nasa to advance  research into flight and the u.s space  program  before his success he was already well  known in aviation  he shot down 13 german planes during  world war ii  five on a single mission he commanded  fighter squadrons  and flew 127 combat missions during the  vietnam war  during the 1960s he trained air force  personnel to become astronauts  26 people he tutored later went into  orbit under nasa  his image as an aviation legend gained  greater status in tom wolf's  best-selling book and later film  the right stuff sounds dangerous it's  very dangerous  he later said one of his regrets was not  going to college  as not having a degree prevented him  from becoming an astronaut  he never regarded himself as courageous  or a hero  often saying he was just doing his job a  job that experts say  led to new heights in aviation and space  exploration
 

